# Normalise to LF in the repository regardless of the platform a commit came from.
#
# This is not tidiness. The workflow files carry multi-line `run:` shell blocks, and a CRLF landing
# in one of those breaks on a Linux runner in ways that read as a mysterious CI failure rather than
# as a line-ending problem. Rego and .mjs are equally happy either way, but a mixed tree makes every
# diff noisy, which is its own cost on a repository meant to be read.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The pinned FedRAMP sources are hashed byte-for-byte in vendor/fedramp/PINNED.json. Any line-ending
# translation on these files would change the hash and fail `npm run vendor:verify`, so they are
# never touched.
vendor/fedramp/** -text

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
